WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.367
-You look gorgeous.
Welcome back.

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:04.300
-I feel like such a letdown
after Dolly.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:05.734
I can't even --
-Oh, stop.

00:00:05.734 --> 00:00:07.133
Oh, come on. No.

00:00:07.133 --> 00:00:08.501
I mean, how ama--
I know, we were --

00:00:08.501 --> 00:00:09.634
You were freaking out backstage.

00:00:09.634 --> 00:00:11.601
-I know, but I just feel --

00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:14.033
I mean, I'm so happy
that she was sat here.

00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:15.234
[ Laughter ]

00:00:15.234 --> 00:00:17.033
-She's sitting in the same --
Oh, stop it.

00:00:17.033 --> 00:00:19.434
-No, I'm just -- I'm so sorry.
For real.

00:00:19.434 --> 00:00:21.601
-[ Laughter ]
-Well, you're a big music fan.

00:00:21.601 --> 00:00:22.868
We were talking last time.

00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:24.801
You were saying how much
you love Bruce Springsteen.

00:00:24.801 --> 00:00:26.200
-Every time I'm here.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.901
-Yeah, and then you were going
to go see him in Broadway.

00:00:28.901 --> 00:00:30.367
-Yeah, but I didn't, no.

00:00:30.367 --> 00:00:34.200
'Cause I very stupidly gave
my ticket to my mother.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:37.834
-Oh, you're so nice.
No, don't make that face.

00:00:37.834 --> 00:00:39.200
You're so happy. You're the
nicest daughter in the world.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.701
-I mean,
she's great, she's great,

00:00:40.701 --> 00:00:42.701
but, yeah, no, I regret it.

00:00:42.701 --> 00:00:44.267
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.267 --> 00:00:45.868
-But you were saying also that
I think,

00:00:45.868 --> 00:00:47.601
it's your favorite
Christmas song as well.

00:00:47.601 --> 00:00:49.634
-Oh, yeah, "Santa Claus Is
Coming to Town."

00:00:49.634 --> 00:00:51.133
-♪ You better watch out ♪

00:00:51.133 --> 00:00:52.801
-The live version when he starts
laughing though.

00:00:52.801 --> 00:00:54.234
-Yes. Oh.

00:00:54.234 --> 00:00:55.801
"Hey, Ben, you been good
this year?"

00:00:55.801 --> 00:00:57.534
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.534 --> 00:00:59.501
-I love it.
-Look, fans of "The Crown,"

00:00:59.501 --> 00:01:01.701
by the way, got very excited
because you had a cameo.

00:01:01.701 --> 00:01:04.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:04.033 --> 00:01:06.734
Come on, buddy. You came back.

00:01:06.734 --> 00:01:08.267
You came back and gave us
a little treat.

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:09.734
-They literally can't get
rid of me.

00:01:09.734 --> 00:01:11.934
-No, we were so happy to see it.

00:01:11.934 --> 00:01:14.267
But I don't think
anyone was excited as --

00:01:14.267 --> 00:01:16.767
You know who was the biggest fan
of you is Nicki Minaj.

00:01:16.767 --> 00:01:18.734
And I'm going to read you
a quote.

00:01:18.734 --> 00:01:20.634
-I know. You're all laughing.
It's ridiculous.

00:01:20.634 --> 00:01:22.033
-[ Laughter ]
-I'm going to read you

00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:23.601
a quote from Nicki Minaj.

00:01:23.601 --> 00:01:26.834
She said, "I can't get enough of
Claire Foy's perfect face.

00:01:26.834 --> 00:01:29.534
I want to eat it."
-[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.534 --> 00:01:32.634
"It just does the right thing
in every single scene."

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:34.601
Aw, she loves your face.

00:01:34.601 --> 00:01:36.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:38.367
Nicki Minaj wants to
eat your face.

00:01:38.367 --> 00:01:40.734
-I would totally let her
eat my face.

00:01:40.734 --> 00:01:42.501
-You would let Nicki Minaj
eat your face?

00:01:42.501 --> 00:01:44.601
-She could try --
I mean, she'd gnaw a bit.

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:46.267
-She could gnaw on it,
yeah, of course.

00:01:46.267 --> 00:01:48.701
But also, you know, what I was
thinking, is maybe you can

00:01:48.701 --> 00:01:51.067
rap with Nicki because last time
you were here, you rapped.

00:01:51.067 --> 00:01:53.100
-Yes, I was forced to.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:55.667
-I politely asked you to.
-[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.667 --> 00:01:57.200
-You were like this
with a microphone.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.968
-Yeah. Do it, do it, do it.

00:01:58.968 --> 00:02:01.701
-It was, like, the most
terrifying thing I've ever done.

00:02:01.701 --> 00:02:02.968
-But you did Sugarhill Gang.

00:02:02.968 --> 00:02:04.801
You did -- It was amazing.
-By muscle memory.

00:02:04.801 --> 00:02:06.400
I wasn't really there
in the room.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:09.334
I was floating above myself,
going, "What are you doing?"

00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:10.501
What's wrong with you?"
-[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.501 --> 00:02:13.100
-"What are you doing?
You have a great career.

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:14.634
Why are you doing this?"
-"Why are you ruining it?"

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:15.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.767 --> 00:02:17.167
-But you did it,
and you crushed it.

00:02:17.167 --> 00:02:18.501
Everyone loved it.
-Hey.

00:02:18.501 --> 00:02:21.901
-Nicki, just saying --
-Oh, my God, Nicki.

00:02:21.901 --> 00:02:23.968
Don't ruin your career by
letting me anywhere near it.

00:02:23.968 --> 00:02:26.234
-[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my gosh.

00:02:26.234 --> 00:02:27.868
Can we talk about --

00:02:27.868 --> 00:02:30.868
You're fantastic, yet again,
in a movie this time.

00:02:30.868 --> 00:02:33.133
This is "Women Talking."
-Yes.

00:02:33.133 --> 00:02:36.033
-It's already --
-[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:36.033 --> 00:02:38.133
-Very good.

00:02:38.133 --> 00:02:40.033
-It's getting awards buzz
already.

00:02:40.033 --> 00:02:42.400
This is based on the book
by the same name.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:45.567
What was your first reaction
to the story?

00:02:45.567 --> 00:02:50.133
-So, it's actually --
Yeah, it's a book written by

00:02:50.133 --> 00:02:51.701
a Canadian author called
Miriam Toews,

00:02:51.701 --> 00:02:55.167
but it's based on a set of
real-life events that happened

00:02:55.167 --> 00:02:58.200
in a Mennonite colony in Bolivia

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:02.767
where women from the ages of 4
to, you know, 90 were waking up

00:03:02.767 --> 00:03:05.701
and having no memory, and it
turned out that they were being

00:03:05.701 --> 00:03:08.133
sexually abused by
men of the colony.

00:03:08.133 --> 00:03:10.701
So that's what the base --
Oh, God, it's really --

00:03:10.701 --> 00:03:13.901
It's a downer, but that's what
the book is based on, that,

00:03:13.901 --> 00:03:16.033
but then the film is
based on the book.

00:03:16.033 --> 00:03:20.167
And it sounds incredibly intense
and hard and difficult,

00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:21.868
but actually the film is
really tender

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:24.200
and full of love
and hope and stuff.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:25.868
-Yeah, it's a very difficult
conversation.

00:03:25.868 --> 00:03:29.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:29.167 --> 00:03:31.200
It's done very, very well.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:33.901
And I will say there's one scene
in particular,

00:03:33.901 --> 00:03:35.367
where you're doing
this monologue

00:03:35.367 --> 00:03:37.200
and you're crushing it.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:40.100
And I read somewhere --
am I making this up? --

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:41.901
it was like 100 takes
or something?

00:03:41.901 --> 00:03:46.501
-We did the first big section of
it 120 times.

00:03:46.501 --> 00:03:49.367
-Maybe on the 50th take, do you
go, "I think we got this one"?

00:03:49.367 --> 00:03:50.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.801 --> 00:03:53.334
-No, because what would happen
is we'd do a day and a half

00:03:53.334 --> 00:03:55.267
on one side, and everyone would
go, "Oh, thank God."

00:03:55.267 --> 00:03:57.934
And then they'd go "turning
round" and the cameras would go

00:03:57.934 --> 00:03:59.701
to the other side, and we'd just
look at the other actors and go,

00:03:59.701 --> 00:04:02.200
"I'm so sorry.
You've got to do it all again."

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:03.701
-You have to do it again.
-Yeah.

00:04:03.701 --> 00:04:06.334
-Oh, my goodness.
-But it was great.

00:04:06.334 --> 00:04:08.400
Amazing actors.
Watching amazing acting.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:09.934
-The whole movie, everyone,
the cast.

00:04:09.934 --> 00:04:12.200
I mean, amazing performances.
-Really amazing.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:14.601
-But, in particular, Claire Foy.
I'm just saying.

00:04:14.601 --> 00:04:16.634
-He has to say that.
-[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:16.634 --> 00:04:18.267
-Just saying.
-Just saying.

00:04:20.801 --> 00:04:24.467
-A couple scenes, you're doing
this incredibly dramatic work

00:04:24.467 --> 00:04:26.968
and then you're going
from crying to laughing.

00:04:26.968 --> 00:04:28.901
And I go, "Who can do that?"
That was very impressive.

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:31.601
-Well, the crying is easier than
the laughing.

00:04:31.601 --> 00:04:33.367
We were all quite scared about
doing the laughing

00:04:33.367 --> 00:04:34.801
because we knew that
we had to do it.

00:04:34.801 --> 00:04:36.234
And you know, like, when you
watch something and someone's

00:04:36.234 --> 00:04:38.067
laughing and it's not quite
reaching their eyes.

00:04:38.067 --> 00:04:39.767
That's the fear of an actor
'cause it's like,

00:04:39.767 --> 00:04:41.000
"I'm not finding this funny
at all

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:42.100
and I'm being made to laugh."

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:44.133
But they didn't have
Rooney Mara,

00:04:44.133 --> 00:04:46.467
who, turns out, she's a genius.

00:04:46.467 --> 00:04:49.033
We were all sat there doing
this scene, and we're thinking

00:04:49.033 --> 00:04:50.634
"It's coming up, it's coming,
it's coming up."

00:04:50.634 --> 00:04:53.234
And then somebody broke wind.

00:04:53.234 --> 00:04:55.434
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.434 --> 00:04:56.701
But we did the nervous thing
of like,

00:04:56.701 --> 00:04:57.934
[ Laughing nervously ]

00:04:57.934 --> 00:05:00.667
"Someone's actually just farted
in the scene."

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:03.234
But it turns out Rooney had
brought a fart machine in,

00:05:03.234 --> 00:05:04.667
and she was sat there going...

00:05:05.434 --> 00:05:07.033
-[ Laughter ]
-Like, with the fart machine

00:05:07.033 --> 00:05:08.033
picking the moment when we could
all laugh.

00:05:08.033 --> 00:05:09.534
-No.
-Yeah, it was amazing.

00:05:09.534 --> 00:05:11.334
-Oh, not bad.
That's how you did it?

00:05:11.334 --> 00:05:13.534
-Yeah. Really recommend
the fart machine.

00:05:13.534 --> 00:05:14.901
-Rooney, good job.

00:05:14.901 --> 00:05:16.467
-Yes, good job, Rooney.

00:05:16.467 --> 00:05:18.601
-I'm so happy every time
you come here. Please come back.

00:05:18.601 --> 00:05:20.167
Congrats on the great reviews
on this.

00:05:20.167 --> 00:05:21.334
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:21.334 --> 00:05:24.133
Here's Claire Foy
in "Women Talking." Take a look.

00:05:24.133 --> 00:05:26.968
-We must consider this.
-No. No.

00:05:26.968 --> 00:05:29.634
That is not our responsibility
because we aren't in charge of

00:05:29.634 --> 00:05:32.100
whether or not
they are punished.

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:36.334
We know that we've been attacked
by men, not by ghosts or Satan,

00:05:36.334 --> 00:05:37.868
as we were led to believe
for so long.

00:05:37.868 --> 00:05:41.133
We know that we've not imagined
these attacks.

00:05:41.133 --> 00:05:44.200
That we were made unconscious
with cow tranquilizer.

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:48.634
We know that we are bruised
and infected and pregnant

00:05:48.634 --> 00:05:53.033
and terrified and insane,
and some of us are dead!

00:05:53.033 --> 00:05:55.767
We know that we must protect
our children

00:05:55.767 --> 00:05:58.968
regardless of who is guilty.

00:05:58.968 --> 00:06:03.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:03.734 --> 00:06:05.367
-Claire Foy, everybody.

00:06:05.367 --> 00:06:08.901
"Women Talking" is
in select cities December 23rd

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:10.801
and nationwide in January.

